     1	# Reproducible assurance runs
     2	
     3	An assurance result is reproducible only when the run records the exact inputs
     4	and execution environment that produced it. A report copied without its run
     5	manifest is an incomplete result.
     6	
     7	## Run manifest
     8	
     9	Initialize `${RUN_DIR}/run-manifest.json` before phase one with the schema, package, adapter,
    10	workspace, and frozen input hashes. Result fields are appended at finalization; the completed
    11	manifest has this shape:
    12	
    13	```json
    14	{
    15	  "schemaVersion": "contract-assurance-run/v2",
    16	  "runId": "2026-11-12-example",
    17	  "createdAt": "2026-11-12T12:00:00Z",
    18	  "package": {"name": "contract-first-assurance", "version": "1.5.2"},
    19	  "adapter": {
    20	    "name": "vformation",
    21	    "version": "1.5.2",
    22	    "requiredGates": ["full-suite", "consumer", "pit", "independent-review", "docs"],
    23	    "acceptedDispositions": {
    24	      "EXPECTED_MUTATION_LIVENESS": {
    25	        "allowedRawStatuses": ["TIMED_OUT"],
    26	        "requiredEvidence": [
    27	          "repeatable-focused-rerun",
    28	          "unmutated-tests-pass",
    29	          "complete-xml-and-logs",
    30	          "source-level-liveness-invariant",
    31	          "maintainer-or-independent-review"
    32	        ]
    33	      }
    34	    }
    35	  },
    36	  "workspace": {
    37	    "base": "<resolved commit>",
    38	    "head": "<resolved commit>",
    39	    "dirty": false
    40	  },
    41	  "finalHead": "<resolved commit>",
    42	  "status": "pass",
    43	  "requiredGates": ["full-suite", "consumer", "pit", "independent-review", "docs"],
    44	  "checks": {
    45	    "full-suite": "pass",
    46	    "consumer": "pass",
    47	    "pit": "pass",
    48	    "independent-review": "pass",
    49	    "docs": "pass"
    50	  },
    51	  "inputs": {
    52	    "inputs/contract-source.md": "<sha256>",
    53	    "inputs/pit-audit.md": "<sha256>"
    54	  },
    55	  "commands": [
    56	    {
    57	      "phase": "full-suite",
    58	      "argv": ["mvn", "test"],
    59	      "exitCode": 0,
    60	      "stdout": "logs/full-suite.stdout.log",
    61	      "stderr": "logs/full-suite.stderr.log"
    62	    }
    63	  ],
    64	  "artifacts": {
    65	    "contract.md": "<sha256>",
    66	    "contract-gaps.md": "<sha256>",
    67	    "candidate-status.csv": "<sha256>",
    68	    "promotion-status.csv": "<sha256>",
    69	    "verification-summary.md": "<sha256>",
    70	    "report.md": "<sha256>",
    71	    "logs/pit.stdout.log": "<sha256>"
    72	  },
    73	  "acceptedExceptions": [
    74	    {
    75	      "phase": "pit",
    76	      "rawStatus": "TIMED_OUT",
    77	      "disposition": "EXPECTED_MUTATION_LIVENESS",
    78	      "accepted": true,
    79	      "evidence": {
    80	        "repeatable-focused-rerun": ["logs/pit.stdout.log"],
    81	        "unmutated-tests-pass": ["logs/pit.stdout.log"],
    82	        "complete-xml-and-logs": ["logs/pit.stdout.log", "inputs/pit-audit.md"],
    83	        "source-level-liveness-invariant": ["inputs/pit-audit.md"],
    84	        "maintainer-or-independent-review": ["inputs/pit-audit.md"]
    85	      },
    86	      "approvedBy": "maintainer"
    87	    }
    88	  ]
    89	}
    90	```
    91	
    92	Rules:
    93	
    94	- `base`, `head`, and `finalHead` are full resolved 40-character SHA-1 or 64-character SHA-256
    95	  commit IDs, never symbolic refs alone;
    96	- `adapter.requiredGates` is the resolved route's required-gate list; gate names are non-blank
    97	  and unique, the top-level `requiredGates` matches it, and `checks` contains a result for every gate;
    98	- `inputs` is non-empty and contains only frozen files whose declared and resolved paths remain
    99	  beneath `inputs/`; the `inputs/` directory itself and any path to a root output or another run
   100	  directory MUST NOT be a symbolic link;
   101	- a dirty workspace must include its binary patch under `inputs/`;
   102	- every copied contract, API view, adapter, command log, promotion record, promoted test copy,
   103	  and report is hashed;
   104	- every promoted row also requires a passing `regression-tests` gate and successful exact-argv
   105	  command records for `regression-metadata`, `regression-tests`, and `regression-execution`, with
   106	  those argv values frozen in `adapter.regressionSuite`;
   107	- every promoted target has a `promotionTargets` entry and a hashed, byte-identical frozen copy at
   108	  `promotion-targets/<target_path>` beneath the configured suite root;
   109	- command records preserve the exact argv, exit code, stdout path, and stderr path;
   110	- paths in the manifest are relative to `${RUN_DIR}` and must not contain `..`;
   111	- a timeout, missing log, missing hash, or hash mismatch makes the run
   112	  `INCONCLUSIVE`, never successful;
   113	- an accepted exception may make the final gate `pass`, but only when its raw
   114	  status, disposition, evidence, and approver are recorded and the disposition is
   115	  allowed by the resolved host adapter; every declared disposition, including an unused one,
   116	  MUST have non-empty, non-blank, unique `allowedRawStatuses` and `requiredEvidence` lists;
   117	  map every required evidence category to existing paths, and hash those paths under `inputs` or `artifacts` so
   118	  `verify_run.py` can enforce the policy without reading a mutable parent checkout;
   119	- frozen metadata, input snapshots, and their hashes are written before tests run and are never
   120	  rewritten; `status`, `requiredGates`, `checks`, `acceptedExceptions`, command results, and
   121	  final-artifact hashes are appended at finalization, including for failed or inconclusive runs.
   122	
   123	## Required layout
   124	
   125	```text
   126	${RUN_DIR}/
   127	├── run-manifest.json
   128	├── inputs/
   129	├── logs/
   130	├── contract.md
   131	├── contract-gaps.md
   132	├── candidates/
   133	├── candidate-status.csv
   134	├── promotions/
   135	├── promotion-status.csv
   136	├── reverse-verification/
   137	├── verification-summary.md
   138	└── report.md
   139	```
   140	
   141	Run `scripts/verify_run.py --run-dir <run-dir>` after the final report. The
   142	verifier checks required artifacts, relative paths, command logs, input hashes,
   143	output hashes, and the report's final-gate consistency without contacting a remote
   144	service. A report whose final gate is not `PASS` or `PASS WITH ACCEPTED EXCEPTIONS`
   145	fails this delivery verifier even when its failure evidence is complete.

