 succeeded in 0ms:
     1	# Mutation dispositions
     2	
     3	Mutation verification has two independent outputs:
     4	
     5	1. the raw status emitted by the mutation runner; and
     6	2. the assurance conclusion after evidence review.
     7	
     8	Never change the raw status in XML, copied reports, or metrics. A raw
     9	`TIMED_OUT` may be accepted as an exception only when the host adapter allows
    10	the disposition and the run records all of the following:
    11	
    12	- the same mutant reproduces the timeout in a focused rerun;
    13	- the unmutated production tests pass;
    14	- XML, command logs, and process-heartbeat evidence are complete;
    15	- the source-level invariant or interleaving that the mutant breaks is stated;
    16	- no worker, memory, or environment failure explains the timeout instead; and
    17	- a maintainer or independent reviewer approves the classification.
    18	
    19	Use this representation in `run-manifest.json` and `report.md`:
    20	
    21	```json
    22	{
    23	  "rawStatus": "TIMED_OUT",
    24	  "disposition": "EXPECTED_MUTATION_LIVENESS",
    25	  "accepted": true,
    26	  "evidence": {
    27	    "repeatable-focused-rerun": ["logs/pit.log"],
    28	    "unmutated-tests-pass": ["logs/pit.log"],
    29	    "complete-xml-and-logs": ["logs/pit.log", "inputs/pit-audit.md"],
    30	    "source-level-liveness-invariant": ["inputs/pit-audit.md"],
    31	    "maintainer-or-independent-review": ["inputs/pit-audit.md"]
    32	  },
    33	  "approvedBy": "maintainer"
    34	}
    35	```
    36	
    37	The final assurance gate may be `pass` when every exception is accepted and every other
    38	required check passes. This does not rewrite a repository-specific PIT report
    39	that separately retains an `inconclusive` raw-run label; it adds the assurance
    40	layer needed to express that the remaining raw timeouts are understood and
    41	accepted. Reports should show this as `PASS WITH ACCEPTED
    42	EXCEPTIONS` for readers while storing the normalized gate value `pass` for
    43	machine checks. An unresolved or weakly evidenced timeout remains
    44	`inconclusive`; increasing the timeout or relying on Maven's exit code is not
    45	an acceptance disposition.

